  "result": "Fixed. `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py` moved the wrong way for open bounds. It returned `bound - dir`, so with `min_open=True` a value below the range clamped to `min - 1`, which is still outside the range. With `max_open=True` it clamped to `max + 1`. It now returns `bound + dir`, so open bounds clamp to `min + 1` and `max - 1`.\n\nI added two cases to the clamp parametrization in `tests/test_types.py`: `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turns `-1` into `1`, and `IntRange(0, 5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` turns `9` into `4`. I only ran `tests/test_types.py` (43 passed, 2 skipped), not the full suite, and I didn't confirm that the new cases fail without the fix.\n\nI didn't touch `CHANGES.md` or `docs/`, which `CLAUDE.md` asks to update for user-visible changes.",
